export const WIKI_PAGES: Record<string, string> = {
 "welcome": "# Welcome to XI: Forever Offline\n![](banner_1)\nXI: Forever Offline (XIFO for short) is an offline, single-player take on classic-era FINAL FANTASY XI. The whole world runs on your own PC: a 75-era server based on Phoenix (a fork of LandSandBoat), a launcher, and Ashita add-ons.\n\n## What it adds\n- **Squad**: up to six persistent party members with their own jobs, levels, gear and roles. See [Squad mates](squad).\n- **A living world** (optional): town crowds, adventuring parties and bot players. See [The living world](living-world).\n- **Co-op and The Hub**: visit friends' worlds or the always-online official world, and bring everything home. See [Co-op & The Hub](coop-hub).\n- **Hardcore modes**: Iron, Steel, Silver and Randomized. See [Hardcore modes](hardcore).\n- **Tetra Master** and the **Crystal Boy**: card games and a Game Boy inside FFXI.\n- A simulated auction house, a living conquest map, era-accurate experience, treasure caskets, fast travel and more.\n\n## Get it\nRead [Getting started](install), or grab the newest version from the NEWS tab.\n\n*XI: Forever Offline is an unofficial fan project, not affiliated with or endorsed by Square Enix. FINAL FANTASY XI © SQUARE ENIX CO., LTD.*\n",
 "install": "# Getting started\n![](banner_5)\n## What you need\n- Windows 10 or 11 (Linux and the Steam Deck: see [Linux & Steam Deck](linux)).\n- A legitimately installed FINAL FANTASY XI. The project never includes Square Enix's game files.\n- Update the game once through PlayOnline (a free trial account works). After that you play offline.\n\n## Install\n1. Download **XI-Forever-Offline.zip** (NEWS tab > GET XIFO, or the GitHub releases page).\n2. Unzip it anywhere, for example `C:\\XIForeverOffline`.\n3. Run **XI Forever Offline.exe** and follow the setup. It finds your game, then downloads Ashita, the server, a small database and the add-ons you pick, all from their official sources.\n4. Pick your world: Quiet world, Living world, or Living world + AI chat.\n5. Press **PLAY**.\n\n## Updates\nThe launcher asks you when a new version is out. Want test builds before everyone else? Turn on *Get test builds* in Settings > Updates.\n\n## Stuck?\nAsk in the Discord's help channels, or post in #bug-reports with your version, what happened and a screenshot or log.\n",
 "squad": "# Squad mates\n![](banner_4)\nYour squad is up to six persistent party members who play alongside you. Each has their own job, level, gear and role, and is controlled by their own AI.\n\n## How they work\n- Mates are **level synced** to your character, so they always fit your fights.\n- They get the **same experience** as any player in the party would, once per kill.\n- **Gear**: trade a piece of gear to your mates once, and the whole squad can use it.\n- **Gambits**: ordered rule sets decide what your mates do in a fight.\n- Squad mates travel with you to co-op worlds and The Hub, and can heal your friends' mates there too.\n\n## Hardcore characters\nHardcore characters have their own squads, managed from the Hardcore menu. Mates never lose levels, even in Steel mode.\n",
 "living-world": "# The living world\n![](banner_2)\nPick **Living world** at setup and Vana'diel fills up.\n\n- **Town crowds**: players standing around towns and outposts, chatting, selling and looking for parties.\n- **Field parties**: groups of adventurers fighting at real camps (they won't take monsters right next to you).\n- **Bot players**: real characters who level from level 1, craft, fish, run battlefields, do quests and missions, use the auction house and run their own linkshells. They keep progressing while you're away.\n- They'll /tell and invite you if your job fills a gap. You can invite them, /tell them, and add your favourites to your friend list.\n- **Bazaars**: what sellers shout in town is real. You can buy the item, or sell to them for gil.\n\n## AI chat\nWith **Living world + AI chat**, bots talk through a local AI model (Ollama) on your own PC. Without it they still chat from a large hand-made dialogue pack.\n",
 "coop-hub": "# Co-op & The Hub\n![](hub)\nYour world is yours, but you can still play together. Everything your character earns somewhere else comes home with it.\n\n## The Hub\nThe official world of XI: Forever Offline, always online, with era rates and bot players. It is always at the top of the CO-OP page. Pick it and press VISIT.\n\n## Friends' worlds\n- **Host**: on the CO-OP page, HOST MY WORLD. Friends get an invite code (like KUPOMG-482-TRX).\n- **Visit**: type the code under VISIT A FRIEND and press PLAY. Next time their world has its own card: one click.\n- Works on the same network, over Tailscale or over the internet.\n\n## Open worlds\nHosts can open their world to anyone. Open worlds are listed on the CO-OP page with their banner, description and how many people are there. Some have a password, and some take hardcore characters only.\n\n## Good to know\n- Your squad mates come with you and are real party members.\n- Your place in an open world (linkshell, auction house, delivery box) is kept for 90 days after your last visit.\n- A crash or disconnect is harmless: press PLAY THERE again. If a world has been out of reach for 24 hours, **TAKE BACK** brings your character home.\n- Everyone in The Hub gets a white \"Forever\" linkpearl to chat with that world.\n",
 "hardcore": "# Hardcore modes\n![](hc_cards)\nPress **HARDCORE** (beside DUALBOX) and pick a mode before your character's first level. Its rates are locked to that mode's profile wherever it goes: your world, co-op worlds and The Hub.\n\n## Every hardcore mode\nNo auction house, no bazaars, no trades or deliveries with other characters. Squad gear only by trading it to your mates.\n\n## Iron\n![](hc_iron)\n1x experience. Dying works like normal. Parties with anyone, and can step down to a regular character.\n\n## Steel\n![](hc_steel)\n2x experience. No Home Point or Survival Guide teleports. Parties only with hardcore characters (your squad, no bot players). A Steel character that is knocked out sends **that job back to level 1**. Everything you completed stays, and squad mates keep their levels.\n\n## Silver\n![](hc_silver)\n3.5x experience, the same limits as Steel. A Silver character that is knocked out is **gone**: it rests on the memorial and is deleted 7 days later.\n\n## Randomized\n![](hc_random)\nYou pick the name; race, looks, nation and your starting job are rolled. More jobs are rolled as you level, loot is randomized (but still fits), and you start with a random level 1 gear set and 10,000 gil. Not hardcore: trading and the auction house are allowed, and it parties with anyone.\n\n## Milestones\nEvery 10 levels on a job, random cosmetics arrive in your delivery box: 1 for Iron, 2 for Steel, 3 for Silver. Milestones, Steel falls and Silver deaths are announced in your world, on The Hub and in Stinkshell (switch it off in the Hardcore menu). Each mode's shield shows beside your name.\n",
 "character-pages": "# Character pages & the Armory\n![](banner_4)\nYour characters can have their own page on xiforever.com: your face, race and nation, your jobs, everything you're wearing, your crafts and fishing, your fame and your squad.\n\n## Put your characters on the site\n1. In the launcher, open the **Characters** page.\n2. Press **SYNC NOW**. Each of your characters gets a page at xiforever.com/c/Name.\n3. Switch on **Update my character pages when I press STOP** to keep them up to date.\n\n## Who can see it\nPick a character on the Characters page and choose:\n- **Everyone**: in the Armory list and the Hall of Fame.\n- **Only people with the link**: not listed; share the link yourself.\n- **Nobody**: hidden.\n\nGil and what's in your bags are never shown on the site. The first player to sync a name keeps it.\n\n## The Armory and the Hall of Fame\n- **xiforever.com/armory**: browse and search everyone's characters.\n- **xiforever.com/armory/fame**: the highest levels, the most jobs at 75, the best anglers, the longest adventures, the hardcore runs still standing, and the Silver memorial.\n\n## On your phone\nPress **PAIR APP** in the launcher and type the code in this app's **ME** tab. Your phone then shows your characters, hidden ones too, with your gil.\n",
 "portable-fishing": "# Portable fishing\n![](banner_3)\nFish on your phone with one of your real characters. Everything you catch comes home to them.\n\n## Get started\n1. Pair this app with your launcher (ME tab) and press **SYNC NOW** in the launcher.\n2. Open **FISH**, pick your character, then a region, a place and a spot. These are the game's real fishing spots, with the fish that really live there.\n3. Pick a rod and bait, and **Cast**.\n\n## The fight\nWhen something bites, arrows appear. Tap the matching side (**◀** or **▶**) before the arrow goes away. Every right tap tires the fish out; a wrong or slow one gives it strength back. Wear it down before the time runs out. Gold arrows mean a critical bite: easier to land.\n\n## Skill\nSkill-ups follow the server's own rules, starting from your character's real fishing skill. Your guild rank still caps it: rank up at the Fishermen's Guild in the game to go further. The world's fishing skill-up rate (or your hardcore mode's) applies here too.\n\n## Rods and bait\n- **Rods**: the fishing rods your character owns. No rod? The guild lends you a Willow Fishing Rod.\n- **Bait**: a free starter pack, the bait in your character's bags, or buy more in the **Tackle Shop** with your character's gil. Lures are never used up.\n\n## Getting it home\nYour catches are sent to xiforever.com as you fish (or with **Send now**). At your next **PLAY** the launcher takes them in before the game starts:\n- the fish and items arrive in your **delivery box**,\n- your fishing skill goes up,\n- gil you spent on bait comes off, and gil you fished up is added,\n- the bait you used from your bags is taken out.\n",
 "stinkshell": "# Stinkshell chat\n![](banner_3)\nStinkshell is one online chat room for every XI: Forever Offline player, whatever world you play in. It's in the game, on xiforever.com and in this app.\n\n## In the game\n1. Switch **stinkshell** on at OPTIONS > Addons. It needs the internet and the launcher open.\n2. **/stink** opens or closes the window.\n3. **/sl text** says something without opening it.\n\nYour screen name is your character's name. The first player to use a name keeps it, and anyone else gets a number after it.\n\n## Who's who\n- In game: the character's name.\n- Website: **website: Name**\n- This app: **mobile: Name**\n\n## Rules\nBe nice. Moderators can mute, kick and ban. In this app, long-press a name to block someone (only you stop seeing them). Trouble with someone? Tell a moderator on the Discord.\n",
 "tetra-master": "# Tetra Master\n![](banner_4)\nThe PlayOnline card game, inside FFXI, with art by Nalfey.\n\n- Start with **Luto Mewrilah** in Upper Jeuno: she hands out your starter deck.\n- Card traders in each area's tavern sell starter cards.\n- Collect 250 cards from card traders, monsters and treasure caskets. The good ones are rare.\n- Play the computer for gil. Type **/tm** to open it.\n",
 "crystal-boy": "# The Crystal Boy\n![](banner_1)\nA Game Boy you earn in game and play inside FFXI.\n\n- Bluffnix's Gobbiebag quests give you the **Crystal Boy** and cartridges: recollections of past adventures found in crystals.\n- Finish a game and hand it in to Bluffnix for rewards: a key item that gives **+1% experience** while Signet is active, a Page from the Dragon Chronicles, an Anniversary Ring and gil.\n- It has controller support, fast forward and save states.\n- Bring your own ROMs if you want the classic games. None are included.\n",
 "linux": "# Linux & Steam Deck\n![](banner_2)\n**Experimental.** The server, the database and the launcher run natively on Linux. The game runs through Proton, which the launcher downloads and keeps in its own folder. Nothing is installed system-wide and nothing needs sudo.\n\n## What you need\n- A 64-bit Linux from 2022 or newer (SteamOS 3.5+, Bazzite, Fedora 37+, Ubuntu 22.04+, Arch, Mint 21+).\n- About 25 GB free.\n- Your updated **SquareEnix** game folder (copied from a Windows PC, or the game installed on Linux).\n\n## Install\n1. Download **XI-Forever-Offline-Linux.tar.gz** and extract it (Steam Deck: in Desktop Mode).\n2. Run **XI-Forever-Offline** in the folder.\n3. The setup asks for the game folder, your world and an account, then downloads what it needs.\n\n## Steam Deck\nLauncher: **SYSTEM > Linux > Add to Steam and the menu**, then start it from your library in Game Mode.\n",
 "help": "# Help & the Discord\n![](banner_3)\n## Found a bug?\nPost it in the Discord's **#bug-reports** forum, one bug per post:\n- What happened, and what you expected\n- Steps to make it happen again\n- Your version (Settings > Updates shows it)\n- Your world (Quiet / Living / Living + AI)\n- A screenshot or log\n\n## Ideas\nPost them in **#suggestions**, one idea per post. Say what you'd like and why it fits the era.\n\n## Join the project\nTesters, developers (Lua, C++, Python), artists and writers are all welcome. Pick your roles on the Discord and say hi.\n\n## Support the devs\nSee #support-the-devs on the Discord, or catch the streams on twitch.tv/hurami.\n"
};
